Once Functional requirements are captured - system is a blackbox  [System has inputs and outputs]
Blackbox =  has a Behavior and a well defined interface

interface is a contract between Engineers who implement the system and client applications who use the system
interface is called by other applications and referred to as an Application Programming Interface (API)
The API are called remotelt via a Network
   Frontend clients - Mobile applications , web browser
   Bankend Systems  - that belong to other companies
   Internal systems - within an organisation
Each component of the system will have its own API

API Categories
 Public APIs   - open for public use for developers , need to register before allowing to send request and use system
    Control of who uses the system externally
    Control on how to use the system
    Better Security
    Blacklist users breaking the rules
 Private APIs
   Exposed Internally in the organisation
   Take advantage of other systems
   Provide bigger value for the company
   not exposing system external the organisation
 Partner APIs
  Similar to public APIs exposed to company / user with business relationship
  Customer agreements after buying product / service
Complete Encapsulation *
  abstract it away from a developer wanting to use the system
  require any info about implemented system , want to know about business logic of the application
  encapsulation is crucial for defining clear and consistent interfaces. By exposing only essential methods and hiding implementation details
APIs should be decoupled from internal design and implementation
   Fullfil 
     One way to get certian data / perform task
     Descriptive names for actions and resources
     Expose only information and actions that users need
     Consistency across the API
   Operations Idempotent
     An operation doesn't have any additional effect on the results if it is performed more than once
 API Pagination *
   responce from the system to the client request contains a very large payload or dataset
   Purpose , allow request only a small segment of the response , specify the max size of each response from the system , specify an offset within the overall dataset
     to receive the next segment we increment the offset [OFFSET] Page-Based and Cursor-Based
Asynchronous Operations
    When an operation needs one big result at the end
    nothing meaningfull can be provided before the entire operations finishes
Versioning API is best practice 
Best Practice
  Complete Encapsulation
  Ease of use
  Making our operations idempotent
  API pagination
  Asynchronous Operations
  API versioning
